            <div class='post' itemprop="text">
              <p><strong>Bulletin ID:</strong> HCSEC-2026-03<br>
<strong>Publication Date:</strong> March 12, 2026</p>
<p><strong>Summary</strong><br>
<em><strong>This bulletin is for informational purposes only. HashiCorp published signatures can be verified using the same public key as previously, and there should be no external action required.</strong></em></p>
<p>The GPG key for <a href="mailto:security@hashicorp.com">security@hashicorp.com</a> (<code>C874011F0AB405110D02105534365D9472D7468F</code>), used to sign binaries on <a href="http://releases.hashicorp.com" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">releases.hashicorp.com</a>, is set to expire on April 18th, 2026. The key has been updated to expire on March 1st, 2030. The latest version of the public key can also be obtained <a href="https://www.hashicorp.com/.well-known/pgp-key.txt" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">here</a>.</p>
<p><em>We deeply appreciate any effort to coordinate disclosure of security vulnerabilities. For information about security at HashiCorp and the reporting of security vulnerabilities, please see <a href="https://hashicorp.com/security" rel="noopener nofollow ugc">https://hashicorp.com/security</a>.</em></p>
            </div>

